 it is added to the message header, including technical details, such as who created the message and the software used to compose it.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="80016">message header</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ne-NP"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1880408">P2 हेडर</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NPL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14999_80016_487419"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A hidden section of an email message. From the time a message is first created, information about it is added to the message header, including technical details, such as who created the message and the software used to compose it.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="80016">message header</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ne-NP"><ntig><termGrp><term id="487419">सन्देश शीर्षलेख</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NPL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1500_7883_486886"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Pertaining to an entity such as the device, program, file, record or portion of the screen that is currently operational or subject to command operations.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="7883">active</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ne-NP"><ntig><t