der's identity to the information being sent. A digital signature may be bundled with any message, file, or other digitally encoded information, or transmitted separately. Digital signatures are used in public key environments and provide authentication and integrity services.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="298008">signature</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ne-NP"><ntig><termGrp><term id="488407">हस्ताक्षर</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NPL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7054_764_486790"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Data that binds a sender's identity to the information being sent. A digital signature may be bundled with any message, file, or other digitally encoded information, or transmitted separately. Digital signatures are used in public key environments and provide authentication and integrity services.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="764">digital signature</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ne-NP"><ntig><termGrp><term id="486790">डिजिटल हस्ताक्षर</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NPL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7054_764_488407"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Data that binds a sender's identity to the information being sent. A digital signature may be bundled with any message, file, or other digitally encoded information, or transmitte